lcats/experimental/secrets_hygiene/scratch/

# Ignore genre-census per-story checkpoint state (internal resume cache,
# redundant with the committed census_*_stories.jsonl/summary.json).
# Targets the checkpoint file's own fixed name (run_census.py's
# "genre_census" stage) rather than every subdirectory - a blanket
# results/*/ pattern would also ignore a candidate-scoped results
# subdirectory's own real committed output (review finding, PR #292).
experiments/04_genre_census/results/**/genre_census.json

# Ignore WI-PILOT-0067 stability-gate per-story checkpoint sidecars.
# The committed evidence is the gate's JSON/JSONL/Markdown report files
# directly under results/stability_gate/; checkpoint subdirectories are
# local resume/debug state produced by run_pilot.py.
experiments/03_cross_segment_relation_pilot/results/stability_gate/fixtures__*/

# Ignore WI-GENRE-0004/WI-LLM-0074 --validate per-story checkpoint state
# (internal resume cache, redundant with the committed
# validation_results.jsonl/validation_summary.json/validation_run_log.jsonl
# and their backend/model/endpoint-qualified equivalents). WI-LLM-0074's
# checkpoint-collision fix (_validation_checkpoint_stage()) qualifies the
# checkpoint filename itself by backend/endpoint (e.g.
# validation_openai_http_localhost_11434_v1.json), so the pattern must
# match that family, not just the literal "validation.json".
#
# A fixed */*/ depth (an earlier version of this pattern) assumed
# --output was always two levels below results/ (results/full_scan/...)
# - but --output defaults to results/ itself, one level shallower, so a
# default-output real run's checkpoints went unignored (review finding:
# Codex P2, PR #361). Matched by directory *name* instead of a fixed
# depth: checkpoint files always sit directly under a
# _validation_item_id()-named directory (row["story_id"].replace("/",
# "__"), always exactly one literal "__" - e.g. "sherlock__five_orange_
# pips"), which the real evidence files (validation_summary.json etc.,
# sitting directly in the experiment's own output directory, never
# inside a "__"-named directory) never match regardless of --output's
# own depth. Same targeted-filename approach as the genre-census pattern
# above (not a blanket results/*/ pattern, for the same PR #292 reason).
experiments/05_metadata_genre_prefilter/results/**/*__*/validation*.json

# Ignore WI-LINGUISTICS-0007 regenerated copied story buckets and expanded JSON
# sidecars. The committed pilot evidence is the report/audit metadata plus the
# compact Parquet export under results/parquet/.
experiments/09_rich_linguistics_genre_sample/results/copied_buckets/
